# earth.png IS COMMITTED. It used to be ignored here and that was a bad call.
#
# The reasoning was that the land texture derives from an outside land-cover map
# and this repository is public, and the consoling line was "the game falls back
# to the untextured globe without it, so a fresh clone still runs". It does run.
# It also ships with a vanilla globe, silently, because gijoe_globe_earth.rul
# does nothing at all when the file is absent and says nothing about it.
#
# Nothing in .github/workflows regenerates it, so EVERY Windows build made from
# this repo had a plain globe. John found that by playing it, which is the
# expensive way to find out. An asset the game needs does not belong in
# .gitignore on the strength of a fallback that hides its absence.

# Ten ORIGINAL X-COM tilesets, same reason: derivative of the game's own art.
# Everything in mod/TERRAIN with a Joe, Cobra or North-America name is ours
# and is committed.
#
# MARS is Cydonia's, not Destro's M.A.R.S. - the name collides and the file
# does not.
#
# THIS COSTS NOTHING, which was not obvious and had to be measured. The
# recolour is not artwork: the geometry is untouched, same frame count, same
# 32x40 tiles, every pixel in the same place, and only the palette index each
# pixel carries differs. ONE table of index -> index reproduces all of it -
# 180,480 pixels compared across the four tilesets a partial data install
# could be checked against, with no pixel contradicting it.
#
#   python3 -I build/recolor_terrain.py <X-COM TERRAIN> mod/TERRAIN --write
#
# derives that table from the player's own game data, refuses if any pixel
# disagrees with it, and rebuilds these ten. It is proven on UFO1, U_BITS,
# U_EXT02 and U_WALL02, which regenerate to exactly the files the mod shipped.
# The other six are not in this container's partial data and the script
# reports them as unproven rather than assuming them.
mod/TERRAIN/BRAIN.*
mod/TERRAIN/MARS.*
mod/TERRAIN/UFO1.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_BASE.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_BITS.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_DISEC2.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_EXT02.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_OPER2.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_PODS.*
mod/TERRAIN/U_WALL02.*
